    "text": "1. Import the supermarket sales dataset into Power BI and iden\u019ffy the data types of each column.\n2. Create a Card Visual to display:\n3. \uf0b7 Total Sales\n4. \uf0b7 Total Quan\u019fty Sold\n5. \uf0b7 Average Customer Ra\u019fng\n3. Create a Clustered Column Chart showing Total Sales by Branch .\n4. Create a Bar Chart showing Total Sales by Product Line .\n5. Create a Pie Chart showing the percentage distribu\u019fon of Payment Methods .\n6. Create a Donut Chart showing the distribu\u019fon of Customer Type (Member vs Normal) .\n7. Create a Column Chart showing the Total Quan\u019fty Sold by Product Line .\n8. Create a Line Chart to display Daily Total Sales using the Date field.\n9. Create a Line Chart showing Monthly Sales Trend .\n10. Create a Stacked Column Chart comparing Sales by Branch and Customer Type .\n11. Create a Stacked Bar Chart showing Product Line Sales by Gender .\n12. Create a Treemap displaying Sales Contribu\u019fon of Each Product Line .\n13. Create a Sca\u01a9er Chart showing the rela\u019fonship between Unit Price and Quan\u019fty , with bubble size represen\u019fng Total Sales.\n14. Create a Histogram (or grouped column chart using bins) for Customer Ra\u019fngs .\n15. Create a Table Visual displaying:\n19. \uf0b7 Invoice ID\n20. \uf0b7 Branch",
