    "text": "21. \uf0b7 Product Line\n22. \uf0b7 Quan\u019fty\n23. \uf0b7 Total\n24. \uf0b7 Payment\n16. Create a Matrix Visual showing:\n26. \uf0b7 Rows: Branch\n27. \uf0b7 Columns: Product Line\n28. \uf0b7 Values: Total Sales\n17. Create a Gauge Chart comparing:\n30. \uf0b7 Value: Average Ra\u019fng\n31. \uf0b7 Target: 8.0\n18. Create a Ribbon Chart showing the ranking of Product Lines by Sales across Branches .\n19. Create a Funnel Chart showing Sales by Payment Method .\n20. Create a Map Visual displaying total sales by City .\n21. Add a Slicer for:\n36. \uf0b7 Branch\n37. \uf0b7 City\n38. \uf0b7 Product Line\n39. \uf0b7 Payment Method\n40. \uf0b7 Gender\n22. Create a dashboard containing:\n42. \uf0b7 Total Sales Card\n43. \uf0b7 Sales by Branch\n44. \uf0b7 Sales by Product Line\n45. \uf0b7 Payment Method Pie Chart\n46. \uf0b7 Daily Sales Trend\n47. \uf0b7 Customer Ra\u019fng Gauge\n48. \uf0b7 Product Line Treemap\n23. Format all charts by:\n50. \uf0b7 Adding \u019ftles\n51. \uf0b7 Displaying data labels\n52. \uf0b7 Changing colours\n53. \uf0b7 Adjus\u019fng legends\n54. \uf0b7 Applying an appropriate theme\n24. Create a report page that allows users to filter sales by Branch and Product Line using slicers.\n25. Publish the completed Power BI report to the Power BI Service and verify that all visuals work correctly a\u014cer publishing.",
